# {{project}}

{{description}}

An application made with [Yuneta](https://github.com/artgins/yunetas):
its yunos live under `yunos/`, their configurations under `yunos/batches/`.

## Layout

```text
{{project}}/
    CMakeLists.txt          builds yunos/
    yunos/
        CMakeLists.txt      one add_subdirectory() per yuno
        batches/<host>/     the configurations of each node
```

## A new yuno

```bash
cd yunos
yuno-skeleton yuno_citizen          # asks for the role, then the rest
```

then add `add_subdirectory(<role>)` to `yunos/CMakeLists.txt`.

## Build

Register the project once, and the `yunetas` CLI builds it after the SDK:

```bash
yunetas register-project $PWD
yunetas build {{project}}
```

Or by hand:

```bash
mkdir -p yunos/build && cd yunos/build
cmake .. && make install
```

## License

{{license_name}}, see `LICENSE`.

{{project}} is closed; Yuneta, the SDK it is made with, is MIT, and no license
it brings in is copyleft on the code of {{project}}. What a delivery must
carry:

- **The notices of Yuneta.** `LICENSE.txt` and `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES` of the
  yunetas version {{project}} was built with (in the yunetas repository at
  that tag, or `/yuneta/development/yunetas/` on a node installed from the
  package), next to the binaries.
- **Relinking (glibc and argp, LGPL-2.1).** The yunos are static binaries,
  so a client who gets them must be able to relink them with another glibc:
  deliver the source of {{project}}, or its object files and the commands
  that link them. Running {{project}} only on your own servers delivers no
  binary, and asks for none of this.
- **The SPA is always delivered**, to every browser that loads it: serve the
  `licenses.txt` that gobj-ui's `yunetaLicensesPlugin()` writes into
  `dist/`, and link it from the About page (it carries the attribution of
  the Font Awesome icons, which a minified bundle loses).
- **The `LICENSE` of {{project}}** must not forbid what the LGPL allows: a
  clause against reverse engineering, if you add one, leaves glibc and argp
  out, as the `LICENSE` made by this template says.

Ask before delivering a bundle or a binary that carries a GPL or AGPL
component.

